{"id": "biz-5", "headline": "Democrats set to widen probe of Obamacare coverage cancellations", "source": "KFF Health News", "url": "https://kffhealthnews.org/elections/midterms-democratic-wins-aca-obamacare-purge-senate-insurance-investigation/", "published": "2026-11-20", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["A week before the midterms, a dozen Democratic senators wrote to 10 health insurer CEOs asking why they cooperated with what the senators called a potentially unlawful Trump administration effort that cancelled coverage for 760,000 Affordable Care Act enrollees in late August, KFF Health News reports. Democrats' election wins will put them in control of both chambers in January. Sen. Ron Wyden, expected to chair the Finance Committee, leads the inquiry and his office says it will continue. Subpoena power could raise the stakes for insurers, said Georgetown's Katie Keith.", "The cancellations are part of a wider effort to remove people with other coverage and tighten subsidy checks, and courts have blocked some of the new rules. Source: KFF Health News"], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110110000100010011001100110001111111", "10000010110101101110111011000010001000001", "10111010000110111011010111010110001011101", "10111010000100111011111101110111101011101", "10111010101110111011111001100110001011101", "10000010111101101110101010100010101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000101100000010000000111010000000000", "11100110101010011001100010001001111110011", "01111100100000111001101110011011101101001", "11101011110011110111011101010101111101101", "01101000011010111010101010101010001101010", "00101011111011111111100010111010101000011", "01011000101010101010101110011001101100011", "01011110100010101010110110110001101010001", "00100100111110111011100010100011101101000", "11001011001010100000100110011000101101001", "10100100001111011111100111111111101100001", "01110010110100010001110101010101101001101", "11010100101111001100100110111010111011010", "1